  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Client Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the client application\'s structure, focusing initially on feature identification. I\'m starting with the branding, imagining a luxury nocturnal theme, using a deep obsidian palette for the background. This will inform the visual aesthetics of the application.\n\n\n**Refining the Color Palette**\n\nI\'ve finalized the color palette, moving from `#090D16` to `#0F172A` for the primary background. I\'m focusing on bioluminescent teal, dream lavender, deep sleep indigo, circadian gold, and restorative jade for accents. I\'m aiming for smooth gradients and glass-morphic surfaces with high contrast, mathematical balance, and a clear typography hierarchy. I\'m also planning the core application views and capabilities.\n\n\n**Developing Prognostic Tools**\n\nI\'m now focusing on adding predictive capabilities. I\'ve designed a \"Longevity & Health Prognosis Engine\" tab. It features projections for various timeframes and risk modeling across multiple organ systems. I\'m exploring an interactive slider to model health impact based on sleep changes, leveraging dynamic mathematical models. I\'m also planning the design for the third tab, the \"Interventions & CBT-I Clinic\".\n\n\n**Constructing CBT-I Module**\n\nI\'m making progress on the \"Interventions & CBT-I Clinic\" tab. I\'m focusing on crafting the CBT-I features. Currently, I\'m integrating a Sleep Restriction Therapy (SRT) Prescription Engine to optimize Time in Bed (TIB) and Total Sleep Time (TST). I\'m also implementing a Stimulus Control Protocol and a \"20-Minute Reset\" guide. There\'s a cognitive worry journal and reframing tool in development. The goal is to provide validated CBT-I cognitive restructuring.\n\n\n**Implementing Vagal Reset**\n\nI\'m now integrating a sympathetic vagal reset module. I\'ve designed features including physiological sigh guidance and a visual aura ring with auditory cues. I\'m also including a Non-Sleep Deep Rest (NSDR)/Yoga Nidra visual player.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Exporting Swift Code**\n\nThe user specifically requested Swift code for the App Store! I\'m creating a complete, production-ready Swift 5.9/SwiftUI codebase. This includes modules for HealthKit integration, sleep architecture analysis, hypnogram visualization, CBT-I clinical engine, and a SomnaLux widget for iOS 17+. I am also integrating an audio synthesizer.\n\n\n**Adding AI Consultation**\n\nI\'ve incorporated a Gemini AI-powered sleep clinician, accessible via a dedicated tab. This allows users to receive instant interactive consultations and ask specific questions about sleep disorders, supplements, jet lag, or PSG reports. I\'ve designed prompt chips for convenience. I am now exploring PWA capabilities, including the `manifest.webmanifest` file and responsive layouts. Furthermore, I am initiating component construction in the `/src/` directory.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 501690491
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
