  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Apply \"Elegant Dark\" Design Theme:** The user requested the application of a specific \"Elegant Dark\" theme (colors: `#050505` background, `#1E293B` cards, `#2DD4BF` accents, etc.).\n  - **Status:** IMPLEMENTATION (Partial)\n  - **Note:** The theme has been applied to the global CSS, the main `App.tsx` shell, the `Header`, and the `SleepDashboard`. The remaining components (`LongevityPrognosis`, `InterventionsClinic`, `NeuromodulationStudio`, `SwiftCodeStudio`, `AICoachChat`, and `LogSleepModal`) still require styling updates to match this theme.\n  - **Constraint:** \"Do NOT replace or restructure the existing app\'s HTML elements \342\200\224 preserve all existing components, content, and functionality. Only modify CSS/styling and adjust layout containers as needed.\"\n\n2. User Knowledge\n- **Design System:** The user provided the \"Elegant Dark\" theme definition:\n  - Background: `#050505`\n  - Cards/Borders: `#1E293B`\n  - Primary Accent: `#2DD4BF`\n  - Secondary Accent: `#6366F1`\n  - Text: `#F9FAFB`\n- **Constraint:** Strict adherence to preserving existing component structure while applying new styles.\n- **Context:** The application is a React-based PWA with native Swift export capabilities.\n\n3. Work Accomplished\n- **Global Styling:** Updated `/src/index.css` to include base body styles, custom scrollbars, and font settings.\n- **Shell & Navigation:** Updated `/src/App.tsx` to use the new background colors and updated the persistent audio player styling.\n- **Header:** Updated `/src/components/Header.tsx` to use the new color palette, borders, and button styles.\n- **Dashboard:** Updated `/src/components/SleepDashboard.tsx` to use the new theme, including card backgrounds, borders, and accent colors for the charts and metrics.\n- **Why:** These changes establish the visual foundation for the \"Elegant Dark\" theme across the core application entry points.\n\n4. Model Knowledge\n- **Architecture:** React SPA using Tailwind CSS.\n- **Styling Pattern:** The application relies on Tailwind utility classes. The \"Elegant Dark\" theme uses a specific set of hex codes (`#050505`, `#1E293B`, `#2DD4BF`, etc.) that must be applied consistently to `bg`, `border`, `text`, and `shadow` properties.\n- **State Management:** Navigation is handled via `activeTab` state in `App.tsx`.\n- **Constraints:** Must not alter the underlying HTML structure of components; only modify `className` attributes and layout container styles.\n\n5. Files and Code\n- **Edited Files:**\n  - `/src/index.css`: Added base styles, custom scrollbar, and font configuration.\n  - `/src/App.tsx`: Applied theme to the main layout and persistent audio player.\n  - `/src/components/Header.tsx`: Applied theme to navigation and brand elements.\n  - `/src/components/SleepDashboard.tsx`: Applied theme to all cards, gauges, and diagnostic report sections.\n- **Viewed Files:**\n  - `/src/App.tsx`: Main routing and layout.\n  - `/src/components/Header.tsx`: Navigation and branding.\n  - `/src/components/SleepDashboard.tsx`: Main data visualization and diagnostic view.\n\n6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Current Work:** Applying the \"Elegant Dark\" theme to the component suite.\n- **Next Steps:**\n  1.  Systematically apply the \"Elegant Dark\" theme to the remaining components:\n      - `/src/components/LongevityPrognosis.tsx`\n      - `/src/components/InterventionsClinic.tsx`\n      - `/src/components/NeuromodulationStudio.tsx`\n      - `/src/components/SwiftCodeStudio.tsx`\n      - `/src/components/AICoachChat.tsx`\n      - `/src/components/LogSleepModal.tsx`\n  2.  Verify that all components maintain their original functionality and structure while adopting the new visual style."
    included_step_index_start: 58
    included_step_index_end: 72
    conversation_log_uris: "file:///.aistudio/artifacts/brain/6f82293d-2072-4a08-9176-71d773adf6df/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl"
    user_requests: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/assets/.aistudio/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    user_requests: "I would like to build the ultimate sleep app that can monitor, determine impact on longterm health and help alter sleep patterns through various scientifically proven tools. I want it to be comprehensive, eye popping visuals and very intuitive UI. can such an app be made and be unique enough to attract attention in the app store. I want it as a PWA and also swift code,\n\ngoogle/gemma-4-e4b\nThis is an ambitious, but absolutely achievable, vision. The market for sleep apps is saturated (Calm, Headspace, Sleep Cycle already exist), which means that uniqueness will not come from what you build, but from how you combine science, technology, and user experience.\n\nThe short answer: Yes, an app of this scope can be built. To succeed, you must solve a problem the existing apps either ignore or handle poorly.\n\nHere is a comprehensive breakdown of how to structure this \"ultimate sleep app,\" covering its unique selling proposition (USP), technical feasibility across PWA and Swift, and a phased roadmap.\n\n\360\237\214\237 The Concept: Moving Beyond Tracking to Intervention & Prognosis\nExisting apps are great at Monitoring (\"You slept poorly last night\"). Your app needs to be masters of Diagnosis, Prediction, and Proactive Intervention.\n\nUnique Selling Proposition (USP):\nThe Predictive Sleep Coach: Instead of just showing graphs of what happened, your app will use machine learning correlations to predict why you are struggling long-term and prescribe precise, actionable, multi-modal interventions.\n\n\360\237\247\240 Core Features & Scientific Depth (The \"What\")\nTo be truly comprehensive and scientifically validated, the feature set must go deeper than simple tracking:\n\nAdvanced Monitoring:\nSleep Staging Analysis: If you have access to wearable APIs (Apple Health/Google Fit), analyze REM, Deep Sleep, Light Sleep duration, and calculate sleep efficiency (\nTime Asleep\n/\nTime in Bed\nTime Asleep/Time in Bed).\nEnvironmental Correlators: Track external factors: local air quality index (\nAQI\nAQI), barometric pressure changes, and even pollen counts (via location services).\nLong-Term Health Impact Determination:\nBio-Marker Correlation Engine: This is your differentiator. You correlate poor sleep patterns over weeks/months against known health metrics: mood swings (\nPHQ-9\nPHQ-9 integration), cognitive performance scores, and even heart rate variability (\nHRV\nHRV) trends (if wearable data allows). Example output: \"Your low deep sleep correlating with high morning \nHRV\nHRV suggests potential stress-related fatigue.\"\nRisk Scoring: Assign a calculated \"Sleep Health Score\" that improves/declines based on adherence to your advice.\nPersonalized Interventions (The Actionable Part):\nPre-Bed Routine Architect: Based on the previous night\'s diagnosis, the app dynamically builds the next evening\'s routine (e.g., \"Today, focus on calming \nHRV\nHRV: 15 minutes of box breathing + Magnesium Glycinate reminder\").\nCircadian Rhythm Tuning: Advanced light therapy recommendations based on geographic location and time zone changes.\nCognitive Behavioral Therapy (\nCBT-I\nCBT-I) Modules: Integrating structured, guided modules for sleep restriction therapy or stimulus control (must be presented by a vetted coach/script).\n\360\237\216\250 User Experience & Visuals (The \"Feel\")\nThis is where you beat the competition. The design must feel premium, calming, and sophisticated\342\200\224like a luxury medical device rather than a basic tracker.\n\nVisual Language: Deep blues, muted teals, soft gradients, and high contrast for readability in low light. Absolutely no harsh reds or bright alerts.\nData Visualization: Ditch the standard line graphs. Use abstract, beautiful visual metaphors. Instead of \"Deep Sleep was 1 hr,\" show a filling reservoir that is visibly more full than normal. When sleep improves, the visuals should become calmer and more expansive.\nIntuitive Flow: The journey must always flow: Diagnose \n\342\206\222\n\342\206\222 Understand Why \n\342\206\222\n\342\206\222 Intervene \n\342\206\222\n\342\206\222 Improve. Keep navigation simple.\n\360\237\222\273 Technical Feasibility (PWA vs. Swift)\nYou have requested both a PWA and native Swift code. This suggests you need maximum reach and deep functionality.\n\n1. Native Swift (\niOS\niOS) - The Powerhouse\nFor the ultimate, deeply integrated experience, Swift is mandatory for iOS.\n\nWhy: Only native code allows full access to platform health kits (Apple HealthKit), sophisticated background processing, and the ability to render highly optimized, complex UIs required for a \"premium\" feel.\nBest For: The core monitoring, the \nCBT-I\nCBT-I module execution, and any feature that must run reliably in the background while other apps are open (requires careful handling of Apple\'s background task limitations).\n2. PWA - The Reach Extension\nA PWA is excellent for accessibility and breadth.\n\nWhy: It allows users who don\'t want to download a full \"app\" feel, or those using desktop browsers, immediate access. Your core content (educational modules, basic journaling, reading articles) can live here.\nLimitation: PWAs often hit limitations regarding background data fetching, complex background processing, and accessing the deepest levels of system health APIs compared to a native build.\n\360\237\222\241 Hybrid Recommendation: The Phased Approach\nBuild Native First (Swift): Focus 80% of your initial effort on creating the best possible experience in Swift for iOS. This proves out the core, scientifically heavy features (data correlation, advanced visualization).\nUse Cross-Platform Frameworks for Scale: Use React Native or a similar framework to build the Android/PWA shell around this core logic. This allows you to share components and business logic between your React web stack and your mobile wrapper, maximizing development efficiency without sacrificing too much native feel.\n\360\237\227\272\357\270\217 Phased Development Roadmap (How to Avoid Overwhelm)\nDo not try to build everything at once. Build iteratively based on the scientific evidence you can gather.\n\nPhase 1: The Tracker & Educator (MVP - Minimum Viable Product)\nGoal: Prove the core monitoring concept and gain early user data.\nFeatures: Sleep tracking (\nManual entry\n\342\206\222\nWearable Integration\nManual entry\342\206\222Wearable Integration). Basic visualization of sleep stages. Simple educational articles on \"Sleep Hygiene 101.\"\nTech Focus: PWA/React for rapid deployment across web/mobile wrapper; Swift to hook into Apple HealthKit basics.\nPhase 2: The Diagnostician (The Differentiation)\nGoal: Move from reporting data to interpreting it.\nFeatures: Introduce the Correlation Engine. Users see \"Sleep Quality Score\" and a simple diagnosis (\"You are likely battling \nHRV\nHRV dips due to chronic low-grade stress.\"). Implement guided, basic breathing exercises (\nPWA/Swift\nPWA/Swift).\nTech Focus: Complex state management; backend ML model required for correlation scoring.\nPhase 3: The Coach (The \"Ultimate\" Experience)\nGoal: Deliver prescriptive action and long-term change.\nFeatures: Personalized, multi-week intervention plans (\nCBT-I\nCBT-I). Integration of external data sources (\nAQI\nAQI, etc.). Premium subscription model unlocks deep predictive modeling.\nTech Focus: Advanced backend services, sophisticated UI animations, robust user journey management.\n\360\237\216\257 Conclusion: Will it be Unique Enough?\nYes, if you nail the scientific rigor and the visual presentation.\n\nThe uniqueness lies in combining:\n\nScientific Depth (\nHRV\nHRV \n\342\206\222\n\342\206\222 Stress \n\342\206\222\n\342\206\222 Sleep)\nProactive Prediction (Not just recording history)\nPremium Polish (Eye-popping, intuitive design)\nSend a message to the model...\n\n and ensure the UX flow minimizes friction while maximizing long-term engagement."
    user_requests: "Apply the \"Elegant Dark\" design theme to the app.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nDesign name: Elegant Dark\nDesign HTML: <!doctype html>\\n<html style=\\\"height: 100%; margin: 0;\\\">\\n  <head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\" />\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\" />\\n    <script src=\\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@tailwindcss/browser@4\\\"></script>\\n    <link href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Material+Symbols+Outlined:opsz,wght,FILL,GRAD@20..48,100..700,0..1,-50..200\\\" rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" />\\n    <style>\\n      body { margin: 0; height: 100%; display: flex; flex-direction: column; overflow: hidden; }\\n      /* Fallback classes in case Tailwind fails to load in sandbox */\\n      .h-full { height: 100%; }\\n      .w-full { width: 100%; }\\n      .flex { display: flex; }\\n      .flex-col { flex-direction: column; }\\n      .flex-1 { flex: 1 1 0%; }\\n    </style>\\n  </head>\\n  <body>\\n    <div class=\'h-[768px] w-[1024px] bg-[#050505] text-[#F9FAFB] flex flex-col font-sans overflow-hidden p-8\'> <header class=\'flex justify-between items-center mb-10\'> <div class=\'flex items-center gap-3\'> <div class=\'w-10 h-10 bg-gradient-to-tr from-[#6366F1] to-[#2DD4BF] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shadow-[0_0_20px_rgba(45,212,191,0.3)]\'> <div class=\'w-5 h-5 bg-[#050505] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center\'> <div class=\'w-2 h-2 bg-white rounded-full\'></div> </div> </div> <span class=\'text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight\'>AETHER <span class=\'font-light text-[#94A3B8]\'>SLEEP</span></span> </div> <div class=\'flex items-center gap-8\'> <div class=\'flex flex-col items-end\'> <span class=\'text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#64748B]\'>Sleep Efficiency</span> <span class=\'text-xl font-mono text-[#2DD4BF]\'>92.4%</span> </div> <div class=\'w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-[#1E293B] border border-[#334155] flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden\'> <div class=\'w-full h-full bg-gradient-to-b from-[#94A3B8] to-[#475569]\'></div> </div> </div> </header> <main class=\'flex-1 grid grid-cols-12 gap-8\'> <section class=\'col-span-7 flex flex-col justify-center relative\'> <div class=\'absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center pointer-events-none\'> <div class=\'w-[480px] h-[480px] rounded-full border border-[#1E293B] opacity-40\'></div> <div class=\'w-[380px] h-[380px] rounded-full border border-[#334155] opacity-60\'></div> <div class=\'w-[280px] h-[280px] rounded-full border-2 border-[#6366F1] opacity-20\'></div> </div> <div class=\'relative z-10 flex flex-col items-center\'> <div class=\'text-[180px] leading-none font-extralight tracking-tighter text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-[#1E293B]\'> 07<span class=\'text-4xl align-top mt-12 inline-block font-medium\'>H</span>24 </div> <div class=\'mt-[-20px] text-[#2DD4BF] font-mono tracking-[0.4em] uppercase text-sm\'>Optimal Rest Duration</div> <div class=\'mt-8 flex gap-12\'> <div class=\'text-center\'> <div class=\'text-[#94A3B8] text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest mb-1\'>Deep Sleep</div> <div class=\'text-2xl font-light\'>2h 14m</div> </div> <div class=\'text-center border-x border-[#1E293B] px-12\'> <div class=\'text-[#94A3B8] text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest mb-1\'>REM Phase</div> <div class=\'text-2xl font-light\'>1h 48m</div> </div> <div class=\'text-center\'> <div class=\'text-[#94A3B8] text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest mb-1\'>HRV (Avg)</div> <div class=\'text-2xl font-light text-[#818CF8]\'>64 ms</div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section class=\'col-span-5 flex flex-col gap-6 justify-center\'> <div class=\'bg-[#0F172A] border border-[#1E293B] rounded-[32px] p-6 shadow-2xl\'> <div class=\'flex items-center justify-between mb-4\'> <span class=\'text-sm font-medium text-[#F1F5F9]\'>Longevity Prognosis</span> <span class=\'px-3 py-1 bg-[#2DD4BF22] text-[#2DD4BF] text-[10px] uppercase font-bold rounded-full border border-[#2DD4BF44]\'>Predictive</span> </div> <div class=\'flex gap-4 items-end h-24 mb-4\'> <div class=\'flex-1 bg-[#1E293B] rounded-t-lg h-[40%]\'></div> <div class=\'flex-1 bg-[#1E293B] rounded-t-lg h-[65%]\'></div> <div class=\'flex-1 bg-[#6366F1] rounded-t-lg h-[85%] shadow-[0_-5px_15px_rgba(99,102,241,0.4)]\'></div> <div class=\'flex-1 bg-[#2DD4BF] rounded-t-lg h-[95%] shadow-[0_-5px_15px_rgba(45,212,191,0.4)]\'></div> <div class=\'flex-1 bg-[#1E293B] rounded-t-lg h-[70%]\'></div> </div> <p class=\'text-[#94A3B8] text-xs leading-relaxed\'> Current patterns suggest a <span class=\'text-white\'>12% increase</span> in cardiovascular recovery efficiency over the next 3 months if circadian consistency is maintained. </p> </div> <div class=\'bg-[#1E1B4B] border border-[#312E81] rounded-[32px] p-6 relative overflow-hidden\'> <div class=\'absolute top-0 right-0 p-4\'> <svg width=\'40\' height=\'40\' viewBox=\'0 0 24 24\' fill=\'none\' stroke=\'#818CF8\' stroke-width=\'1.5\'> <path d=\'M12 3v1m0 16v1m9-9h-1M4 12H3m15.364-6.364l-.707.707M6.343 17.657l-.707.707m12.728 0l-.707-.707M6.343 6.343l-.707-.707\' stroke-linecap=\'round\'/> </svg> </div> <div class=\'relative z-10\'> <h3 class=\'text-[#C7D2FE] text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest mb-2 font-bold\'>Nightly Protocol</h3> <p class=\'text-xl font-light text-white mb-4 leading-snug\'>Reduce blue light by 20:45. <br/>Lower core temp to 18.5\302\260C.</p> <button class=\'bg-[#818CF8] text-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold hover:bg-[#6366F1] transition-colors\'> Begin Wind-down </button> </div> </div> </section> </main> <nav class=\'h-16 flex justify-around items-center border-t border-[#1E293B] mt-8\'> <div class=\'flex flex-col items-center gap-1 opacity-100\'> <div class=\'w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-[#2DD4BF] rounded-full mb-1 shadow-[0_0_10px_#2DD4BF]\'></div> <span class=\'text-[10px] uppercase tracking-tighter font-bold text-white\'>Discover</span> </div> <div class=\'flex flex-col items-center gap-1 opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity cursor-pointer\'> <span class=\'text-[10px] uppercase tracking-tighter font-bold\'>Trends</span> </div> <div class=\'flex flex-col items-center gap-1 opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity cursor-pointer\'> <span class=\'text-[10px] uppercase tracking-tighter font-bold\'>Health</span> </div> <div class=\'flex flex-col items-center gap-1 opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity cursor-pointer\'> <span class=\'text-[10px] uppercase tracking-tighter font-bold\'>Coach</span> </div> <div class=\'flex flex-col items-center gap-1 opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity cursor-pointer\'> <span class=\'text-[10px] uppercase tracking-tighter font-bold\'>Settings</span> </div> </nav> </div>\\n  </body>\\n</html>\nDesign instructions: Extract ONLY the styling (colors, fonts, spacing, borders, shadows, backgrounds, gradients) and layout patterns (flexbox/grid structure, component arrangement) from the Design HTML above. Do NOT replace or restructure the existing app\'s HTML elements \342\200\224 preserve all existing components, content, and functionality. Only modify CSS/styling and adjust layout containers as needed to match the theme\'s aesthetic. You MUST execute file editing or creation tool calls (such as edit_file, multi_edit_file, or create_file) to apply styling updates to target files directly. Do NOT output code blocks, HTML, or TSX directly in your text chat response.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
