  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Feedback**\n\nI\'m focused on dissecting the user\'s feedback. I\'m taking the criticism point by point, looking specifically at the buttons first. I need to figure out what they mean by \"fully built\" and why the buttons aren\'t working. This is the keystone to the whole process.\n\n\n**Enhancing Interactions**\n\nI\'m now pivoting to user interactivity, specifically in the context of the dashboard. I\'m thinking of making the archetype selector more prominent, possibly with interactive cards for quick selections. I also want to make the diagnostic insights more immediate and interactive, possibly using tabs or toggles. Feedback on all interactive elements will be crystal-clear, with instant visuals and computation. Epoch scrubbing needs more attention too; a click should lock an epoch for detailed EEG insights.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Visuals**\n\nI\'m now integrating an interactive \"What-If\" Sleep Simulator directly into the dashboard. Sliders will let users instantly see how changes in sleep parameters affect their scores. I\'m also planning an interactive \"Science & Mechanism Explorer\" with breakdowns of the core biological pillars, and a 10-Year Health & Disease Risk Prognosis feature with interactive visual risk gauges. This will make the scientific foundations of the app immediately engaging and intuitive.\n\n\n**Designing New Features**\n\nI\'m now focused on incorporating interactive features with real-time scientific citations. I\'m building a dynamic circadian clock wheel, a CBT-I clinic with interactive sleep tools, and an acoustic neuromodulation visualizer. The user interface will see improvements including a clean top navigation with badges, and a \"Clinical Presets\" banner for quick test scenarios.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 243225049
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
